UGC.OS Privacy Policy

Effective Date: July 6, 2026
Last Updated: July 6, 2026

1. Introduction

UGC.OS ("UGC.OS," "we," "us," or "our") provides an AI-powered video content production platform that helps brands and creators plan, generate, and publish user-generated-style content ("Service"). This Privacy Policy explains how we collect, use, disclose, and safeguard information when you use our website, dashboard, and related services (collectively, the "Platform").

By creating an account or using the Platform, you agree to the collection and use of information as described in this policy. If you do not agree, please do not use the Platform.

2. Information We Collect

2.1 Information You Provide Directly


Account information: name, email address, password (hashed), company/brand name, billing details.
Content inputs: briefs, scripts, product descriptions, brand guidelines, images, video clips, and other assets you upload or generate through the Platform.
Persona and voice data: any AI persona configurations, voice samples, or likeness data you create or upload for use in generated content.
Communications: messages you send to support, feedback, or survey responses.


2.2 Information from Connected Third-Party Accounts

If you connect social or marketing accounts (e.g., via our Metricool integration) to schedule or analyze content, we receive:


Account identifiers and profile metadata
Post performance metrics (impressions, engagement, reach)
Publishing permissions you grant to those platforms


We only access what is necessary to provide scheduling, publishing, and analytics features, and only with your explicit authorization (typically via OAuth).

2.3 Information Collected Automatically


Usage data: pages visited, features used, workflow steps completed, timestamps, click data.
Device and log data: IP address, browser type, operating system, referring URLs.
Cookies and similar technologies: used for authentication, session management, and (where applicable) analytics. See Section 8.


2.4 AI-Generated Content Data

When you use the Platform to generate video, audio, or image content, inputs and outputs may be processed and temporarily or persistently stored (via our infrastructure, including Supabase-hosted databases and storage, and third-party AI/render providers) to deliver the Service, enable revisions, and maintain your content library.

3. How We Use Information

We use collected information to:


Provide, operate, and maintain the Platform, including content generation, scheduling, and publishing workflows.
Authenticate accounts and manage multi-tenant access and permissions.
Process payments and manage subscriptions.
Generate analytics and insights about content performance.
Improve and train internal tooling and workflow logic (not to train third-party foundation models beyond what those providers' own terms permit — see Section 5).
Communicate with you about updates, support, and service-related notices.
Detect, prevent, and address fraud, abuse, or security issues.
Comply with legal obligations.


We do not sell your personal information.

4. Legal Bases for Processing (EEA/UK Users)

Where applicable, we process personal data under one or more of the following bases: performance of a contract, your consent, our legitimate interests (operating and improving the Platform, security), and compliance with legal obligations.

